---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const mcpConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "dollarlint": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": "dollarlint",
      "args": ["serve", "mcp"],
      "tools": ["*"]
    }
  }
}`;
---

<DocsLayout title="CLI reference" current="/reference/cli/">
  <article class="doc">
    <header class="doc-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Reference</span>
      <h1>CLI reference</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The full ledger of commands and flags for validating files, creating
        configs, and checking what you've got installed.
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>Commands</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dollarlint validate [path]</code></td>
          <td
            >Validate files under a path. Defaults to the current directory if
            you don't specify one.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dollarlint init [path]</code></td>
          <td
            >Mint a starter <code>.dollarlint.toml</code> in the target directory.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dollarlint serve mcp</code></td>
          <td
            >Start a Model Context Protocol server over stdio so agents can
            validate files with DollarLint.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dollarlint version</code></td>
          <td>Print the installed version. Quick sanity check.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dollarlint completion</code></td>
          <td>Generate shell completion scripts through Cobra.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Global flags</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Flag</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--config</code></td>
          <td
            >Use an explicit <code>.dollarlint.toml</code> path. Relative paths are
            resolved from the validation root, or beside an explicit file target.</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--version</code>, <code>-v</code></td>
          <td>Print the installed version.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Validate flags</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Flag</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td><code>--format</code></td><td
            >Choose <code>text</code>, <code>json</code>, or <code>sarif</code>.
            Defaults to <code>text</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--output</code>, <code>-o</code></td><td
            >Write output to a file instead of stdout. Use <code>-</code> or omit
            it for stdout.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--locations</code></td><td
            >Include line and column positions in text and JSON output. SARIF
            requests source locations automatically.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--verbose</code></td><td
            >Show expanded issue metadata in text output.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--quiet</code></td><td
            >Use terse success text output and omit the summary details from
            failing text output.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--show-skipped</code></td><td
            >Show files skipped because they do not declare or match a schema.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--include</code></td><td
            >Set discovery include globs. Repeatable; when provided, replaces
            config includes for this run. A glob without a slash can match a
            basename at any depth.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--extend-exclude</code></td><td
            >Add a discovery exclude glob on top of config and built-in default
            excludes. Repeatable. A glob without a slash can match a basename at
            any depth.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--no-default-excludes</code></td><td
            >Disable built-in discovery excludes.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--no-gitignore</code></td><td
            >Do not apply <code>.gitignore</code> patterns during discovery.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--force-exclude</code></td><td
            >Apply excludes even to explicitly passed files.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--schema</code></td><td
            >Associate a file glob with a schema as <code>glob=uri</code>.
            Repeatable. Association globs use the same slashless-basename
            behavior as discovery globs.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--schema-store</code></td><td
            >Match conventional filenames using the SchemaStore catalog.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--schema-store-url</code></td><td
            >Use a SchemaStore-format catalog URL or local path and enable
            catalog matching.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--schema-store-failure</code></td><td
            >Set catalog failure policy to <code>warn</code>, <code>error</code
            >, or <code>skip</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--max-depth</code></td><td
            >Set maximum external schema reference depth.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--fetch-remote</code></td><td
            >Allow fetching HTTP schemas. Defaults to enabled; pass <code
              >--fetch-remote=false</code
            > to disable.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--no-schema-cache</code></td><td
            >Disable the disk cache for remote schemas and catalogs.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--fetch-retries</code></td><td
            >Set retries for transient remote schema fetch failures. Defaults to <code
              >2</code
            >.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--allow-domain</code></td><td
            >Allow remote schemas from a domain. Repeatable.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--block-domain</code></td><td
            >Block remote schemas from a domain. Repeatable.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--fetch-timeout</code></td><td
            >Set schema fetch timeout, such as <code>10s</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--compile-timeout</code></td><td
            >Set schema compile timeout, such as <code>30s</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Branch-error reporting is configured in <code>.dollarlint.toml</code>
      rather than a validate flag. Use <code>output.branchErrors = "best"</code>
      for focused <code>oneOf</code>/<code>anyOf</code> diagnostics, or <code
        >"all"</code
      > when debugging every failed schema branch.
    </p>

    <h2>Init flags</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Flag</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td><code>--output</code>, <code>-o</code></td><td
            >Path to the <code>.dollarlint.toml</code> file to create.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--force</code></td><td
            >Overwrite an existing config file.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--defaults</code></td><td
            >Skip prompts and use defaults plus provided flags.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--fetch-remote</code></td><td
            >Allow fetching HTTP schemas in the generated config. Pass <code
              >--fetch-remote=false</code
            > to disable.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--fetch-retries</code></td><td
            >Set generated retry count for transient fetch failures. Defaults to <code
              >2</code
            >.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--schema-store</code></td><td
            >Enable the built-in SchemaStore catalog in the generated config.
            Defaults to enabled.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td><code>--schema-store-failure</code></td><td
            >Set generated catalog failure policy to <code>warn</code>, <code
              >error</code
            >, or <code>skip</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>MCP server</h2>
    <p>
      <code>dollarlint serve mcp</code> starts a stdio MCP server. It is meant to
      be launched by an MCP client, not run directly in a terminal session.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{mcpConfig}</code></pre>
    <p>
      The server exposes one tool, <code>validate</code>, with one optional
      argument: <code>include</code>. Pass file or glob patterns relative to the
      server working directory to narrow validation for a tool call, or omit it
      to use configured discovery. The tool includes source locations
      automatically and returns structured JSON with <code>ok</code>, <code
        >message</code
      >, and the regular DollarLint <code>result</code> payload.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
